    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "but it doesnt feel like a weight i can just \"work through\" with a therapist. it feels more like... a design flaw. like i'm a machine built to malfunction. if the blueprint is already broken, how is talking about it supposed to fix the hardware? it feels like i'm just delaying the inevitable.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of being fundamentally flawed is deeply isolating, and it's understandable why therapy might feel inadequate against such a deep-seated sense of doom. Instead of trying to \"fix\" the hardware, perhaps you can view it as understanding the design—acknowledging the wiring so you can choose how to interact with it. Sometimes the most profound relief comes not from changing the blueprint, but from accepting the current state and finding ways to make it bearable, even if it's not perfect.",
      "source": "target",
